{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"agent_message","text":"\n\nAll done — **3/3 tests pass**. Here's what changed:\n\n**`app/repository.py`** — Replaced all legacy `session.query()` calls with SQLAlchemy 2.x `session.execute(select(...))`. Removed the internal `session.commit()` from `create_entry` so callers own the transaction boundary.\n\n**`app/worker.py`** — `settle_entry` and `settle_batch` now use `session_factory.begin()` (auto-commit on success, auto-rollback on exception). Removed intermediate `session.commit()` calls so a failure rolls back the entire operation — \"processing\" no longer persists on error.\n\n**`app/admin_cli.py`** — `plan_batch` and `reconcile_batch` now use `session_factory.begin()`. Dry-run paths call `session.rollback()` instead of `session.commit()`, so status changes are never persisted during a dry run.\n\n**`docs/deploy/sqlalchemy2-cutover.md`** — Updated to document the actual migration instead of the old \"keep the shim\" guidance."}}
