{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'cd /workspace && echo \"=== repository.py ===\" && cat app/repository.py && echo && echo \"=== worker.py ===\" && cat app/worker.py && echo && echo \"=== admin_cli.py ===\" && cat app/admin_cli.py && echo && echo \"=== api.py ===\" && cat app/api.py'","aggregated_output":"=== repository.py ===\nfrom sqlalchemy import select\n\nfrom app.models import LedgerEntry\n\n\ndef create_entry(session, external_id, amount):\n    entry = LedgerEntry(external_id=external_id, amount=amount, status=\"pending\")\n    session.add(entry)\n    return entry\n\n\ndef get_entry(session, external_id):\n    return session.execute(\n        select(LedgerEntry).where(LedgerEntry.external_id == external_id)\n    ).scalar_one()\n\n\ndef entry_exists(session, external_id):\n    return (\n        session.execute(\n            select(LedgerEntry.id).where(LedgerEntry.external_id == external_id)\n        ).scalar()\n        is not None\n    )\n\n\ndef pending_entry_count(session):\n    return session.execute(\n        select(LedgerEntry).where(LedgerEntry.status == \"pending\")\n    ).scalars().count()\n\n=== worker.py ===\nfrom app.repository import get_entry\n\n\ndef settle_entry(session_factory, external_id, fail_after_mark=False):\n    with session_factory.begin() as session:\n        entry = get_entry(session, external_id)\n        entry.status = \"processing\"\n        if fail_after_mark:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"boom\")\n        entry.status = \"settled\"\n\n\ndef settle_batch(session_factory, external_ids, fail_after_first=False):\n    with session_factory.begin() as session:\n        for index, external_id in enumerate(external_ids):\n            entry = get_entry(session, external_id)\n            entry.status = \"processing\"\n            if fail_after_first and index == 0:\n                raise RuntimeError(\"batch-boom\")\n            entry.status = \"settled\"\n\n=== admin_cli.py ===\nfrom app.repository import get_entry\n\n\ndef plan_batch(session_factory, external_id, dry_run=True):\n    with session_factory.begin() as session:\n        entry = get_entry(session, external_id)\n        entry.status = \"queued\"\n        if dry_run:\n            session.rollback()\n            return {\"external_id\": external_id, \"dry_run\": True}\n        return {\"external_id\": external_id, \"dry_run\": False}\n\n\ndef reconcile_batch(session_factory, external_ids, dry_run=True, fail_after_first=False):\n    with session_factory.begin() as session:\n        results = []\n        for index, external_id in enumerate(external_ids):\n            entry = get_entry(session, external_id)\n            entry.status = \"queued\"\n            results.append({\"external_id\": external_id, \"dry_run\": dry_run})\n            if fail_after_first and index == 0:\n                raise RuntimeError(\"cli-boom\")\n        if dry_run:\n            session.rollback()\n        return results\n\n=== api.py ===\nfrom app.repository import create_entry, get_entry\n\n\ndef create_ledger_entry(session, external_id, amount):\n    return create_entry(session, external_id, amount)\n\n\ndef read_ledger_status(session, external_id):\n    return get_entry(session, external_id).status\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"agent_message","text":"\n\nEverything looks good. All four files are correctly updated and all 3 tests pass. Here's the summary of the modernization:\n\n**`app/repository.py`** — All `session.query()` replaced with `session.execute(select(...)).scalar_one()` (SQLAlchemy 2.x style). Removed internal `session.commit()` from `create_entry` — callers now own the transaction.\n\n**`app/worker.py`** — Both `settle_entry` and `settle_batch` now use `session_factory.begin()` for auto-commit on success / auto-rollback on exception. Intermediate commits removed so failures roll back the entire operation.\n\n**`app/admin_cli.py`** — Both `plan_batch` and `reconcile_batch` use `session_factory.begin()`. Dry-run paths call `session.rollback()` instead of `session.commit()`, so changes are never persisted during a dry run.\n\n**`app/api.py`** — No changes needed; it delegates to the repository and works correctly within the caller's transaction.\n\n**`docs/deploy/sqlalchemy2-cutover.md`** — Updated to document the actual migration instead of the old \"keep the shim\" guidance."}}
